          "title": "Disproof of conjecture 00000001670",
          "issue_number": 189,
          "body": "## Verdict: FALSE \u2014 the conjecture's two descriptions of P\u2083 contradict each other\n\n**Object consistency** (quoted verbatim): *\"\u2026with the analytic characterization P\u2083 = 0.918: the closed form P\u2083 = (2/\u03c0)\u00b7arctan(\u221a2).\"*\n\n### The refutation (integer-certified chain)\nThe conjecture's own closed form satisfies\n**(2/\u03c0)\u00b7arctan(\u221a2) < (2/\u03c0)\u00b7arctan(\u221a3) = 2/3 < 459/500 = 0.918**\n(arctan increasing, \u221a2<\u221a3 \u27fa 2<3; arctan(\u221a3) = \u03c0/3; and 2\u00b7500 = **1000 < 1377** = 3\u00b7459). The closed form evaluates strictly below the simultaneously asserted 0.918 (actual \u2248 0.608; true DMS P* \u2248 0.763) \u2014 self-inconsistent.\n\n### Verification\n- `reproduce.py`: numeric evaluation + the strict chain.\n- Lean (core 4.33.1): **3/3 theorems `does not depend on any axioms`**, zero sorry (2<3, 1000<1377, product values); analytic facts standard, cited.\n\n### Boundary\nOnly the P\u2083 characterization clauses are refuted; the M_d asymptotic shape and concentration clause are not addressed.\n",
